<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        ====================================================
        App Attest is currently DISABLED in this entitlement.
        ====================================================

        Why: the App Attest capability requires a PAID Apple
        Developer Program membership ($99/year). The empty
        entitlement set below lets the project build with a
        FREE Apple ID, so you can install on your phone for
        development without paying yet.

        Penumbra was written to degrade gracefully when this
        capability is missing:
          • AttestationManager.swift checks
            `DCAppAttestService.shared.isSupported` and, when
            false, emits a "DEV_…" key-id with a placeholder
            assertion header.
          • The backend's dev-mode path (APP_ATTEST_ENFORCE=0,
            see BUILD_INSTRUCTIONS.txt Step 7) accepts those
            headers without cryptographic verification.

        So with this file as-is + `APP_ATTEST_ENFORCE=0` on
        the backend, the full feature surface works for
        development. You just shouldn't expose that backend
        URL to the public — anyone with it could call your
        endpoints.

        ------------------------------------------------
        TO ENABLE APP ATTEST (paid membership only):
        ------------------------------------------------
        1. Pay the $99/year fee at developer.apple.com
        2. Register your bundle ID with the App Attest
           capability ticked (BUILD_INSTRUCTIONS.txt §1.3)
        3. In Xcode → Signing & Capabilities tab →
           "+ Capability" → add "App Attest"
        4. UNCOMMENT the two lines below
        5. Redeploy the backend with APP_ATTEST_ENFORCE=1
        6. For App Store / TestFlight builds, also change
           "development" → "production" below AND set
           APP_ATTEST_ENVIRONMENT=appattest on the backend.

        <key>com.apple.developer.devicecheck.appattest-environment</key>
        <string>development</string>
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
